#: src/control-flow-basics/blocks-and-scopes.md:6
msgid "Blocks and Scopes"
msgstr ""

#: src/control-flow-basics/blocks-and-scopes.md:8
msgid ""
"A block in Rust contains a sequence of expressions, enclosed by braces `{}`."
msgstr ""

#: src/control-flow-basics/blocks-and-scopes.md:9
msgid ""
"The final expression of a block determines the value and type of the whole "
"block."
msgstr ""

#: src/control-flow-basics/blocks-and-scopes.md:13
msgid "// Copyright 2023 Google LLC\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/control-flow-basics/blocks-and-scopes.md:14
msgid "// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/control-flow-basics/blocks-and-scopes.md:24
msgid "// dbg!(y);\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/control-flow-basics/blocks-and-scopes.md:28
msgid ""
"If the last expression ends with `;`, then the resulting value and type is "
"`()`."
msgstr ""

#: src/control-flow-basics/blocks-and-scopes.md:30
msgid "A variable's scope is limited to the enclosing block."
msgstr ""

#: src/control-flow-basics/blocks-and-scopes.md:35
msgid ""
"You can explain that dbg! is a Rust macro that prints and returns the value "
"of a given expression for quick and dirty debugging."
msgstr ""

#: src/control-flow-basics/blocks-and-scopes.md:38
msgid ""
"You can show how the value of the block changes by changing the last line in "
"the block. For instance, adding/removing a semicolon or using a `return`."
msgstr ""

#: src/control-flow-basics/blocks-and-scopes.md:41
msgid ""
"Demonstrate that attempting to access `y` outside of its scope won't compile."
msgstr ""

#: src/control-flow-basics/blocks-and-scopes.md:43
msgid ""
"Values are effectively \"deallocated\" when they go out of their scope, even "
"if their data on the stack is still there."
msgstr ""
